    "alert_id": "P006_TDF_RENAL",
    "title": "Rising creatinine on TDF in pregnancy",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring for patients on TDF, with screening for signs such as changed urine volume. Creatinine rose from 0.8 to 1.1 mg/dL within 10 weeks of starting TDF, and eGFR is 78. TDF is a known cause of renal toxicity including chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome. Pregnancy itself increases renal blood flow and normally lowers creatinine, making this rise more concerning. The patient has no oedema and urinalysis is normal, which argues against overt TDF nephrotoxicity. However, the upward trend warrants close monitoring. Phosphate is normal, providing some reassurance against Fanconi syndrome.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Repeat serum creatinine and eGFR within 4–6 weeks. Monitor for proteinuria and urinary phosphate. Consider TDF dose review or alternative if creatinine continues rising.",
