    "alert_id": "P006_DTG_RBS_GAP",
    "title": "No baseline or follow-up RBS on DTG",
    "message": "Guidelines note that hyperglycemia among previously non-diabetic adults has been reported with DTG, and recommend performing random blood sugar every 3 months for high-risk patients during the first 12 months. This patient has no recorded baseline or follow-up blood glucose since initiating DTG 10 weeks ago. Pregnancy itself increases insulin resistance, compounding any DTG-related hyperglycemia risk. No diabetes history is documented, but no screening has been performed to detect new-onset hyperglycemia.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Perform a random blood sugar now and repeat every 3 months during the first 12 months of DTG therapy, especially given pregnancy.",
