    "alert_id": "P006_VL_TIMING",
    "title": "Viral load drawn before 6-month schedule",
    "message": "Guidelines state that treatment should be monitored by measuring viral load 6 months after ART initiation and every 6–12 months thereafter. This patient's viral load was drawn at 10 weeks, earlier than the recommended 6-month interval. The result of 89 copies/mL is encouraging but does not replace the scheduled 6-month viral load. A repeat viral load at 6 months is still required per guideline.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "low",
    "recommended_action": "Schedule a repeat viral load at 6 months after ART initiation per guideline, regardless of the early result.",
